title the loom that reads a borrowed number -- %357's named guard is built, and its first run found four sites in two witnesses the prior firings never named
prompt The HUSH seat prompt: roster cold then hot, reds first as standfast, rota row N mod 5, QA on touch, read scope, ListAgents before a file moves; take the next Pond lap under the accrete-only gate boundary. The card named my door: the %357 loom, or its question one layer up.
think LISTAGENTS FIRST, and it answered none reachable, so I named the peer from process state -- Dream running Codex in ~/grain-dream, 107 minutes in, plus an idle elder Claude in ~/grain. Separate trees mean separate indexes, so %291 does not reach across us; my commit stays path-limited regardless.
think ROTA. N=3816 by git rev-list --count HEAD gives row 1, AIR -- law and boundary, whose sense is touch: feel for the boundary under the hand, and where the hand passes through, the boundary was a wish. Row 0 was last lap's, so the arithmetic row advanced by one on its own. The row could not have fit the work better: this lap builds a wall, and its threshold page says a claim of a boundary is tested by pressing on it.
think REDS FIRST. Every row on the living pin reads CLOSED by its last bold marker -- I checked with an awk that reads the LAST marker per row rather than the first, since a row records its repair after its booking. Nothing agent-closable stood, so the constructive door was open.
think THE DOOR I TOOK, and why it beat the other. The card offered two: build the %357 loom, or ask how many unrostered guards are red right now. Lindy-first settles it -- a loom is a standing guard that catches the class forever, where a census is one measurement that goes stale the day after it is taken. The census stays a real door and is now the card's Hush line.
think THE SHAPE, read from history rather than from the row's summary. I pulled the pre-repair spellings out of d540ffc67f and found the file named in a COMMENT above the assertion in one case and nowhere near it in another. So a reading that looked only inside the compared string would have passed two of the three sites %357 repaired. The reach had to be: a literal compared anywhere in an assert line, against any tracked path the same source names anywhere at all.
think THE FLOOR, measured rather than chosen. At a one-digit floor the reading compares 3063 literals and returns 5 sites; at three digits it compares 513 and returns 4. The fifth is the literal 0 matching an empty .gitkeep. One digit costs a sixfold larger join and one false site and buys nothing, since only 5 of the 970 subjects this tree names hold under 100 bytes.
think MY OWN JOIN WAS BROKEN, and the looser floor is what showed it. Reading at one digit returned 113 sites, 109 of them the literal 0 against paths like rye/lib/c -- symlinks to directories that wc -c answers 0 for and that my size table therefore never held. An awk array element that was never set compares equal to both "" and 0, so every unmeasured path matched. The fix is a membership test before the comparison, and the comment above the join now says so. That is the air row's own lesson arriving inside the tool written to teach it: I pressed on the boundary and my hand went through.
think THE VACUUM LEG CAUGHT A SECOND ONE, before anything shipped. The scan counted its sources with `grep -c . file 2>/dev/null || echo 0`, and grep -c prints 0 AND exits 1 when it matches nothing -- so the count became the two-line string "0\n0", the integer test errored to stderr, and the guard printed verdict=ok and exited 0 on an empty source list. The one prose paragraph promising it would refuse a confident wrong zero was false about its own code until the leg that proves it ran.
think WHAT THE FIRST RUN FOUND, and it is not what I expected. Four sites, zero false positives, in two witnesses neither prior firing named: tools/g/gism_j6_provenance_true_witness.rish and tools/g/gism_j6_provenance_receipt_witness.rish, both spelling the length 213 and the SHA-256 of waymarks/date/20260801/20260801-134653_e182-q46-errors-named-green.md -- a THIRD document, which is exactly why %357's class sweep for the two documents it knew about could not see them.
think THE SHARPER DEFECT UNDERNEATH. Both witnesses claim in their own headers to cross-check the app against wc -c and sha256sum, "two tools, one answer". They ran both tools and then compared each answer to the same hand-typed constant, so the two tools never met. And because Rishi's assertion is `contains` rather than equality, `selftest.out contains "signed_len 213"` would be satisfied by a signed_len of 2130 or 21300 -- a substring against a constant accepts any length whose spelling holds it. The repair makes the assertion the comparison: read wc -c and sha256sum first, interpolate both, and the app's answer now meets the filesystem's answer directly.
think PROVEN ABLE TO RED, since a guard that cannot red guards nothing. I pointed the repaired witness's `real` at a 243-byte neighbour on the same shelf and it refused at line 39 with "signed length disagrees with wc -c over the real file". The binding is live rather than decorative.
obs THE READING IS NARROW ON PURPOSE, and its limit is named in its own prose: it catches a pin while the pin is still TRUE, which is the only moment catching it is cheap. Once the document has moved, the literal matches nothing and this guard goes quiet -- by then the witness itself is red, and a red is its own alarm. So the loom and the standing roster close different halves of one class, and the half neither closes is an unrostered guard whose pin has already gone stale. That is the card's Hush door now.
obs FOURTEEN BEHAVIOURS ON A PEN, welcomes as hard as refusals. A borrowed count is found; a borrowed digest named only in a comment is found; the read-and-interpolate repair is NOT counted; a number with no path beside it is free; a size living only in the else message is free, since Rishi prints that string rather than comparing it; a subject under the floor is free; an ambiguous bare basename binds nothing; the ceiling refuses at one and passes at two on ONE pen so the readings differ only in the ceiling; prove-red plants a third and refuses; an empty source list refuses; and outside a repository the scan refuses rather than reading the filesystem.
obs NO RED BOOKED, and the reason is worth writing down. The four sites were GREEN today -- their subject is dated testimony under waymarks/date/, which the one-clock law holds immutable, so the pins were true and had never failed. That is a ratchet, not a red: something not yet uniform, which turns on touch and books nothing. Calling a green witness with a brittle binding a red would spend the word that stops the line on tidiness.
obs WHAT I DID NOT WIDEN. The reading takes Rishi's `assert` alone, because both firings of this class lived there. A Rye selftest spelling another file's facts is outside it, and so is a subject whose path is assembled at runtime. Naming those in the scan's own prose costs four lines and saves the next reader from trusting a reach the guard does not have.
loom witness=borrowed_number wall_s=40 scan_wall_s=14 sources_read=2318 literals_compared=513 subjects_measured=965 digests_measured=119 sites_before=4 sites_after=0
loom roster=cold guards_run=96 guards_green=95 guards_red=1 tree_moved=no red=rule_twin_gate_7
file tools/fixtures/b/borrowed_number_scan.sh the reading -- every tracked Rishi assert line's compared literals joined against the size and digest of every tracked path the same source names, held at a ceiling of zero, with the floor, the else-message exclusion, and the four things it does not reach all argued in its own prose
file tools/fixtures/b/borrowed_number_control.sh fourteen behaviours on real git repositories in a throwaway pen, every welcome asserted as hard as every refusal
file tools/b/borrowed_number_witness.rish the gate -- the living measure, the vacuum refusal, the ceiling from both sides on one plant, and the control's named legs
file tools/g/gism_j6_provenance_true_witness.rish the length and digest are read from disk and interpolated, so the assertion IS the cross-check its header always claimed
file tools/g/gism_j6_provenance_receipt_witness.rish the same repair, and the duplicated cross-check block below it is gone rather than repaired -- re-spelling a number only gives the drift a second home
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the guard seated at tier lap on 40s measured here
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now, the live front, and the Hush door re-aimed; the card trimmed back to 24549 of 24576
recommend check-in (Keaton) -- THE LOOM %357 NAMED IS BUILT AND IT PAID FOR ITSELF ON THE FIRST RUN. `borrowed_number` reads every tracked Rishi assertion for a literal that is exactly the current size or SHA-256 of a tracked file the same source names, and holds that at zero with fourteen behaviours proven on a pen. Its first pass over this tree found FOUR sites in two GISM Journey 6 provenance witnesses that neither %341 nor %357 ever named, because both pin a THIRD document -- which is the whole argument for a loom over a grep: a sweep sees the files it was told about. THE DEFECT UNDER THE DEFECT is sharper than the row that predicted it. Both witnesses promise in their own headers to cross-check the app against wc -c and sha256sum, "two tools, one answer", and both routed the comparison through one hand-typed constant so the two tools never met -- and since Rishi asserts with `contains`, the constant 213 would have been satisfied by a signed length of 2130. Both now read their subject from disk and interpolate, and I proved the repair can RED by pointing it at a 243-byte neighbour. TWO THINGS I OWN. My join first read 113 sites where 4 stand, because an awk array element never set compares equal to 0 and every unmeasured path matched the literal zero; and my vacuum leg found the scan printing verdict=ok on an empty source list, since grep -c prints 0 and exits 1 so the `|| echo 0` beside it made the count two lines. Both are fixed, both are commented where they happened, and the second is why that leg exists at all. NO RED BOOKED -- the four sites were green, their subject is immutable dated testimony, and a brittle binding that has never failed is a ratchet rather than something wrong. YOUR DOOR IS UNCHANGED: `entry` is Pond's last duty and seating it IS the switchover, so it stays your word rather than my lap. MINE NEXT, and the card now names it -- how many unrostered guards are red right now, which is the half this loom cannot see: once a document moves, the borrowed number matches nothing and reads as a bare number, so only running the guard finds it.
